<div class="container">
 
  <!-- SECTION 1: MARKET CONTEXT -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-label">01 · Market Reality</div>
    <h2>The yerba crisis is your buying window</h2>
 
    <p>The INYM deregulation via Milei's DNU 70/2023 stripped the institute of its price-setting powers. The consequences are severe and documented in real-time. Producers are receiving between $160–$220 ARS per kilo of green leaf — while production costs run at $430/kg. That's not a margin squeeze. That's a structural loss on every harvest.</p>
 
    <p>The producer's share of the shelf price collapsed from a historical 23% to roughly 13% today. Many small colonos cannot cover harvest costs and are leaving kilos of hoja verde rotting on the plant. The next logical step is what you're already observing: <strong>forced land sales</strong>.</p>
 
    <div class="data-grid">
      <div class="data-cell">
        <div class="label">Producer price (green leaf)</div>
        <div class="value">$160–220</div>
        <div class="note">ARS/kg. Was ~$400 two years ago</div>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <div class="label">Production cost</div>
        <div class="value">$430+</div>
        <div class="note">ARS/kg — they lose on every sale</div>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <div class="label">Shelf price drop (2023–26)</div>
        <div class="value">−45.7%</div>
        <div class="note">Real terms. Consumer benefits, producer bleeds</div>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <div class="label">Exports 2025</div>
        <div class="value">+7.3%</div>
        <div class="note">57.9M kg / $117M USD. Bright spot for brand play</div>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <div class="label">Land listings (Misiones rural)</div>
        <div class="value">Low</div>
        <div class="note">Supply is rising as colonos sell — prices softening</div>
      </div>
      <div class="data-cell">
        <div class="label">Legal situation</div>
        <div class="value">Fluid</div>
        <div class="note">Federal court challenges pending. Possible partial reversal.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
 
    <div class="verdict-box">
      <div class="verdict-label">Strategic Reading</div>
      <p>A crisis that forces 13,000 small producers to consider selling their chacras is — from a buyer's perspective — a generational pricing window. The land doesn't become less fertile. The water doesn't disappear. The red soil doesn't degrade. What changes is the desperation of the seller. You are positioned to benefit from this if you act with discipline on price and location.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
 
  <!-- SECTION 2: LAND PRICE BENCHMARK -->
  <section>
    <div class="section-label">02 · Land Pricing</div>
    <h2>What $30–50k actually buys you</h2>
 
    <p>Based on current market data from Argenprop, Zonaprop, and Chacras Misioneras, here is the realistic pricing map for rural land in Misiones as of 2026:</p>
 
    <table class="zone-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Zone</th>
          <th>Price/ha (USD)</th>
          <th>25 ha cost</th>
          <th>Your budget fit</th>
          <th>Tag</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Near Posadas / Candelaria corridor</strong><br>On paved road, 20min to capital</td>
          <td>$5,000–$10,000</td>
          <td>$125k–$250k</td>
          <td>Way over budget</td>
          <td><span class="tag tag-avoid">Out of range</span></td>
        </tr>
